module cost_robustness_tradeoff

// PRD v0_6 continuous-cost-minimisation §2.4/§8.1 — the
// `minimize cost_robustness_tradeoff(<money-expr>, λ)` override (task γ #4791).
// Leaf-signal example for the γ decompose slice.
//
// Three structures share the SAME Money cost and the SAME two constraints,
// differing only in λ:
//
//   TradeoffPureCost (λ=1.0) — pure cost-minimisation, floor-free: `thickness`
//     lands on the cost's own closed-form optimum, 5mm.
//   TradeoffBlend    (λ=0.5) — a blend of both anchors: ≈7.19mm, strictly
//     between the two.
//   TradeoffRobust   (λ=0.0) — pure robustness: `thickness` lands on the engine's
//     centrality default — the max-min-slack point, 31/3 mm ≈ 10.33mm — the
//     identical argmax to `build_centrality_objective` by construction (PRD §8.1).
//     NOT the geometric Chebyshev centre; see Lever 2 below for why they differ.
//
// The dial is genuinely observable here — three separated values, none of them
// the solver's own starting guess. Getting there took two deliberate levers,
// one per anchor; both are load-bearing, and removing either collapses the
// sweep back onto a single point (task #5715).
//
// This header OWNS the derivation below. `docs/reify-language-spec.md` §10.8
// and `docs/prds/v0_6/continuous-cost-minimisation.md` §2.4 cite it instead of
// restating it, and the e2e test quotes only the two target values it asserts.
//
// # Lever 1 — why the cost is U-shaped, not monotone
//
// The cost is material-plus-handling shaped: `thickness / 1mm` grows with the
// part, `25mm / thickness` grows as the part gets thinner. As
// `5USD · (a·t + b/t)` with `a = 1/(1mm)` and `b = 25mm`, its unique global
// minimum on `t > 0` is `t* = sqrt(b/a) = sqrt(1mm · 25mm) = 5mm` — STRICTLY
// INTERIOR to the feasible region, so the constraint penalty is identically
// zero around it.
//
// That interiority is the point, and its justification does not depend on any
// solver behaviour: an interior λ=1 optimum is a DIFFERENT POINT from the λ=0
// centrality argmax, so the sweep below can tell the two anchors apart at all.
//
// A MONOTONE Money cost's pure-cost optimum instead lands ON a strict `>`
// boundary — any nonzero cost gradient pushes it there, and the constraint
// penalty has zero slope exactly at its own root (the same characteristic that
// originally motivated the α robustness floor, task #4789). `.ri`-compiled auto
// params always get `bounds: None` (`engine_eval.rs::build_auto_param_list`), so
// `effective_bounds` here is the wide Length default `[1µm, 10m]`; until task
// #6465 nothing else pinned the anchor down and
// `solve_core_with_sd_tolerance`'s "optimizer drifted infeasible
// → fall back to the initially-feasible seed" safety net reported THE SEED. The
// γ regime now derives its own clamp box from the constraints under
// `StrictBound::SteppedInside` (`SolveRegime::TradeoffBlend`, solver.rs),
// because the boundary IS this regime's contracted λ=1 answer — so a monotone
// cost's λ=1 reaches that boundary and is seed-invariant. A strict bound's
// infimum is not attained, so the box stops one representable value inside it
// (task #7883): the λ=1 value satisfies the model's own strict constraint and
// `reify check` passes it. MEASURED at the EVAL layer, monotone
// `5USD · (t/1mm)` under `1mm < t < 4mm`: λ=1 resolves one representable step
// above 1mm, displayed 1.000mm (identically for `auto` and `auto(free)`), λ=0
// the 2.5mm centre.
//
// # Lever 2 — why the upper bound is written `thickness * 2 < 30mm`
//
// It makes the constraint set ASYMMETRIC. The solver seeds a constrained solve
// from the midpoint of a box derived from the constraints, so with a symmetric
// pair such as `1mm < thickness < 15mm` that seed IS the centrality argmax by
// construction — and a λ=0 result landing there proves nothing, since a real
// centrality solve and a drift fallback are indistinguishable at that point.
//
// Two half-spaces with DIFFERENT gradients separate them. The slacks are
// `t − 1mm` (slope +1) and `30mm − 2t` (slope −2); `build_centrality_objective`
// maximises their minimum, so max-min binds them at `t − 1 = 30 − 2t →
// t = 31/3 mm`. The seed is MEASURED, not derived here: the HC4 bound
// derivation (`solver.rs`) reads `thickness * 2 < 30mm` as `thickness < 15mm`,
// so the derived box is `[1mm, 15mm]` and the seed its midpoint, 8mm — pinned
// by `solver.rs`'s `extract_initial_point_seeds_scaled_mul_bound_for_5715_shape`.
// Centrality argmax 10.33mm, seed 8mm: distinct, so the λ=0 anchor is
// checkable.
//
// One precision note on that argmax, and it is load-bearing: it is the
// max-min-RAW-slack point, NOT the geometric Chebyshev centre.
// `collect_slack_terms` folds the slacks un-normalised by each constraint's
// gradient, so the scaled `thickness * 2 < 30mm` weighs double its geometric
// distance: the largest ball inscribed in the feasible region (1mm, 15mm) is
// centred at 8mm, while the engine's centrality default lands at 31/3 mm. λ=0
// must reduce to the ENGINE's default (PRD §8.1), so 31/3 mm is the
// contract-correct target. The old symmetric box made the two coincide, which
// is why the looser "Chebyshev centre" wording was harmless here before task
// #5715 and is not any more. The Chebyshev centre is also exactly the 8mm seed,
// so the raw fold is what keeps the λ=0 anchor off the seed; the e2e test's
// COUPLING CAVEAT says what a normalised-slack reconciliation would cost.
//
// `CentralityReference` is the objectiveless control for exactly that check: the
// same auto param and the same two constraints with NO `minimize` at all, so
// the engine resolves it through its own synthesised `Maximize(min_slack)`
// default (§10.7). It pins the λ=0 target with an ENGINE-COMPUTED value rather
// than a hardcoded constant — the in-example analogue of the solver-level
// sibling's independent `build_centrality_objective` solve.
//
// # Relationship to the PRD §8.1 "λ=1 → boundary" invariant
//
// PRD §8.1's "λ=1 reaches the TRUE constraint boundary, floor-free" is a
// MONOTONE-cost statement: the boundary is where argmin-cost lands when the cost
// has no interior optimum. It is verified rigorously and seed-independently at
// the SOLVER level, with explicit tight `AutoParam` bounds, in
// `crates/reify-constraints/tests/cost_robustness_tradeoff_blend.rs`.
//
// This example demonstrates the more general form the invariant specialises
// from — λ=1 ≡ argmin cost — which is what is observable WITHOUT `AutoParam`
// bounds. Letting `.ri` autos carry bounds (and so making the zero-margin
// boundary form reachable at this layer too) is ζ-gated, not available today:
// `crates/reify-syntax/src/ts_parser.rs`, "δ only PRESERVES these params in the
// AST; consuming them is ζ".
//
// `cost_robustness_tradeoff` REPLACES the α robustness floor for all three
// tradeoff scopes (see
// `crates/reify-eval/src/engine_eval.rs::scope_qualifies_for_robustness_floor`,
// task γ step-08): none of them emit `RobustnessFloorApplied`.
//
// Integration test: crates/reify-eval/tests/cost_robustness_tradeoff_example_e2e.rs
// asserts zero error-severity diagnostics, every value strictly inside the
// feasible region, the λ=1 closed-form cost optimum, the λ=0 centrality argmax
// (both against `CentralityReference` and against the closed-form 31/3 mm), and
// a strictly ordered sweep with a minimum pairwise separation. The two anchor
// targets sit well clear of the 8mm seed — 5mm is 3mm away (300x the test's
// anchor tolerance) and 31/3 mm is 2.333mm away (233x) — so a drift fallback
// onto the seed fails them outright.
//
// # Why auto(free), not strict auto
//
// A strict `auto` triggers the uniqueness check (`solver.rs::verify_uniqueness`).
// That check used to re-solve via the plain `solve_core` path, which — not knowing
// about the `cost_robustness_lambda` marker — would apply the α robustness floor to
// the perturbed re-solve; comparing a floor-free tradeoff-blend solution against a
// floor-adjusted perturbed one (falsely) disagreed, masking the tradeoff signal
// behind a spurious `ConstraintNonUnique`.
//
// Task #5711 CLOSED that hazard for a constraint-BRACKETED model: `verify_uniqueness`
// no longer re-solves for a γ objective at all (the γ dispatch is seed-dependent by
// construction, so a re-solve from a different anchor measures the anchor, not the
// model).  It instead rules on the constraints alone — every strict auto bounded on
// BOTH sides by the user's own constraints is well-determined.  The hazard genuinely
// REMAINS for a model whose strict auto lacks a constraint side: that side then comes
// from `default_bounds_for`, a solver-internal default, and the verdict stays
// `ConstraintNonUnique`.
//
// This example nonetheless stays `auto(free)`, deliberately: the tradeoff behaviour is
// what it exercises, not uniqueness, and flipping it would change an e2e-asserted
// fixture (`crates/reify-eval/tests/cost_robustness_tradeoff_example_e2e.rs`).  Same
// reasoning as `continuous_cost_min.ri`'s "Why auto(free)" block for the plain
// Money-objective floor (task β #4790).
structure TradeoffPureCost {
    param thickness : Length = auto(free)
    param unit_cost : Money = 5USD

    constraint thickness > 1mm
    constraint thickness * 2 < 30mm

    minimize cost_robustness_tradeoff(unit_cost * (thickness / 1mm + 25mm / thickness), 1.0)
}

structure TradeoffBlend {
    param thickness : Length = auto(free)
    param unit_cost : Money = 5USD

    constraint thickness > 1mm
    constraint thickness * 2 < 30mm

    minimize cost_robustness_tradeoff(unit_cost * (thickness / 1mm + 25mm / thickness), 0.5)
}

structure TradeoffRobust {
    param thickness : Length = auto(free)
    param unit_cost : Money = 5USD

    constraint thickness > 1mm
    constraint thickness * 2 < 30mm

    minimize cost_robustness_tradeoff(unit_cost * (thickness / 1mm + 25mm / thickness), 0.0)
}

// The objectiveless control: same auto param, same two constraints, NO
// `minimize`. The engine resolves it through the synthesised centrality default
// (§10.7), so it pins the λ=0 target independently of any tradeoff machinery.
structure CentralityReference {
    param thickness : Length = auto(free)

    constraint thickness > 1mm
    constraint thickness * 2 < 30mm
}
